WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.668
-Now, Halle and I are about
to face off in a game of

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:04.070
"Box of Lies."

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.172
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.440
Here's how it works.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.775
Upstage are a bunch
of boxes containing objects

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:11.310
neither of us have seen before.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.047
Taking turns, we're going
to select a box and open it

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.983
on our side of the table, out of
the view of the other person.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.384
You remove the object
from the box,

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.219
show it to the audience,
our great audience,

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:21.521
then you look
at your opponent...

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.122
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:26.425
...and you tell them
what's in your box.

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:27.560
Then, they have to guess

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.729
if you're lying
or telling the truth.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.497
We'll play three rounds.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.532
Halle, why don't you go
pick the first box.

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:35.601
[ Audience yelling ]

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.370
Yeah, they can help you,
they can help you.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:44.910
[ Audience yelling ]

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.712
Three, interesting.

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:48.047
-Three -- Oh, it's heavy.

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:49.315
-Oh, yeah, right,
it's really heavy.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.616
Please, you're holding it
with one hand.

00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:52.185
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my God.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:53.319
Nice try, already.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.921
That's a hint!
Ha ha, he he.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.089
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.523
Okay, good.

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:59.192
All right.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.694
-Oh, shoot.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:02.862
[ Laughing ]

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.296
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:05.765
Oh.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:10.036
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.271
-I don't know if you --
If you're lying --

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:13.672
I don't know what's happening.

00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:14.940
Already, already, already.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:21.114
-It's -- it's a stuffed animal
of some sort...

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.382
-Okay.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:31.157
With a -- like, a snake
wrapped around it.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.625
With things on its head.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:37.430
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.632
-Now, this is not my first time
I've played this game.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.767
"It's a stuffed animal
of some sort"?

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:44.103
Like, you don't know what
stuffed animal it is?

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.204
-You have to ask that.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.240
-Now, what is it,
like a Hatchimal?

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.975
-No, it's an elephant.
-Or is it like a bear?

00:01:49.975 --> 00:01:52.077
An elephant with a snake
wrapped around its head,

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.714
and things coming out of
the elephant or the snake?

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.082
-The elephant.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:02:01.487
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:05.892
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.928
-I will say, Halle Berry, you...

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.197
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.532
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:15.167
You're telling the truth!

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.235
[ Horn blows ]

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:17.903
-[ Screams ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.173
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:22.108
I knew it,
I knew you were lying!

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.276
[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:25.912
I knew you were lying.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.546
Why did I -- I over thought --
I over thought it.

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:28.815
-[ Imitating horn ]
♪ Waa, waa, waa ♪

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.549
-Oh, my God. Get a life.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:31.884
All right, what number?
What number, I'm up.

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:35.455
[ Audience yelling ]

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:39.058
Someone said ten.
There is no ten!

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.292
Five?

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:43.096
[ Audience yelling ]

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.566
[ Grunting ]

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:48.834
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.437
Okay, here we go.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.805
Okay.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:57.644
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.178
Okay.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:08.721
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.692
[ Cheers ]

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:21.066
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.066 --> 00:03:27.506
All right.

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:28.741
I think I'm just going to have
to tell you the truth

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.009
on this one, I really do.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.411
I just -- I don't think
I can make this one up.

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.644
-It's fine.

00:03:32.644 --> 00:03:35.181
-This is just a --
It's like a pencil sharpener

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:39.786
type of thing where --
Where you put the pencils,

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:43.189
or whatever, you put a --
You put a pretzel stick.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.691
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.691 --> 00:03:47.393
[ Laughing ] In a dude's mouth.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:51.597
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.633
And it sharpens your pencil.

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:56.135
-Sharpens your pencil?

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.570
-Yeah. Or yeah --
I think it looks like that,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.138
it looks like some type of
pencil sharpener, yeah.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.539
-In a dude's mouth?

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:03.242
-You put, like, a pretzel in
a dude's mouth and then a...

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:05.110
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:10.482
[ Laughing ] You call --
You call it a day after that.

00:04:10.482 --> 00:04:12.918
-So, is there a mouth on there?

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:15.388
-Yeah.
-Yeah, there's a mouth on there?

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:20.793
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:24.363
-Is there a dude on there,
like a fake dude?

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.665
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:26.665 --> 00:04:30.136
[ Laughter ]
Sure.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.737
-Okay, I think...

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:32.939
[ Drumroll ]
...you're telling the truth.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:38.044
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:39.678
[ Laughing ]

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:44.183
[ Band plays ]

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.951
-How could I even lie?
After I saw this,

00:04:45.951 --> 00:04:47.953
how could I make up
a lie about that?

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:49.822
It's the most insane thing
I ever seen in my life.

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:52.358
I'm so -- It feels so weird
to have to show that to you.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.094
I'm sorry.
Halle, let's do one more round.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:05:00.600
[ Cheers ]
This is worth 10,000 points!

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.667
Halle, you're up, you're up.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:02.668
Any number.
-Okay.

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:06.072
[ Audience yelling ]

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:10.209
-This is aggressive --
aggressive yelling.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.011
That was an aggressive four.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.646
"Pick four"!

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.715
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.350
-Oh, you might see that.
That's too high.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.252
-Hm.
-I'm going to put this one back.

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:21.321
[ Applause ]
-Oh, see?

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:23.289
I know a magic trick
when I see one.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:25.325
Something just happened.

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:29.862
-Oh, [ bleep ].

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:39.005
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:42.842
This has got
a lot of characters.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.743
-Okay, a lot of
characters involved.

00:05:44.743 --> 00:05:47.579
-A lot of characters involved.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:51.083
Awesome dry cleaning.

00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.251
-And what do you mean,
"dry cleaning"?

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:55.421
What's that mean?

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:56.656
-I don't know.

00:05:56.656 --> 00:06:00.226
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.494
-Oh, my goodness.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.862
I don't even want
to hear anymore.

00:06:03.862 --> 00:06:05.197
I think I can make my decision.

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:06.432
This is -- 'Cause you're good.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:09.435
[ Drumroll ]

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.970
You lie!

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:15.608
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:17.710
[ Laughter ]
[ Horn blows ]

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.078
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:22.615
She's the best right there,
Halle Berry, everybody.

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:23.649
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.384
Thank you for doing that.
You're good.

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:26.753
You are fantastic.

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:28.388
That's why she wins
Academy Awards!

